@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Resume Picker Pinning
+
+- A saved title containing exactly one whitespace-delimited word pins its session above other sessions in the resume picker.
+- Leading and trailing whitespace is ignored.
+- An empty title or a single-word conversation preview does not pin a session.
+- Each group preserves the selected backend time order.
+- One blank row separates the pinned group from the ordinary sessions when both are visible.
+- The separator is not selectable and does not add a second blank row in comfortable view.
+- Existing directory, provider, status and search filters still apply.
+- The first page appears immediately while the picker continues reading existing pagination cursors asynchronously to discover older pinned sessions.
+- Discovery ends at the end of the listing or the existing scan cap.
+- Each arriving page updates the order while preserving the selected session.
+- Title changes made in the picker update the order while preserving the selected session.
+- Titles changed outside the picker are reflected on the next listing reload.
+- Discovering all eligible pinned sessions reads all eligible listing pages without reading their transcripts.
+- The fork picker retains its existing order and on-demand pagination.
